course: dictionary
lesson: 13280
title: Words about government
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from a root word plus an ending. The ending -al turns government into governmental, which describes something that belongs to, or comes from, a government. A government is the group of people who run a country and make its laws. «The governmental plan for new parks was announced today.» The plan comes from the government, so governmental describes it.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. If you know government, you can often work out governmental. «The governmental department checks that schools follow the rules.» Ask yourself: is this part of the government? If yes, the meaning fits.
explain: Some organisations are not run by the government. «The charity is a non-governmental organisation, run by volunteers.» The prefix non- means not, so non-governmental means not run by the government. These groups are often called NGOs.
fact: Governmental means to do with a government.
fact: A government is the group of people who run a country, state or area and make its laws and decisions.
fact: Governmental is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as «governmental policy» or «governmental decisions».
fact: A non-governmental organisation (NGO) is not run by the state, and many charities are NGOs.
fact: The prefix non- means not, so non-governmental means not to do with the government.
exercise: «The governmental department published new figures on schools.» What does governmental mean here? | *To do with the government | Very old and broken | To do with cooking food | Fast and noisy
exercise: «The charity is a non-governmental organisation, run by volunteers.» What does non-governmental mean? | *Not run by the government | Very large and very rich | Run only by children | Run by the government
exercise: Find and copy the one word that means to do with a government: «The governmental policy will change next year.» | year | change | policy | *governmental
test: Which word means to do with a government? | gardening | silently | happiness | *governmental
test: What does the prefix non- mean in non-governmental? | *Not | Again | Very big | Before
exam: «The governmental agency hired new staff, and a non-governmental group helped too.» What does non-governmental mean? | Run by the state | Run by pupils | *Not run by the state | Very quiet
